// KR-89 (consumer KB-32) — the give site is the VARIABLE, not the type. `string b = give a;` then reading
// `a` built clean and answered "" — silently — though the same shape on a `DynamicArray`, an `Owned`, a
// `Shared` or a `Weak` was refused, and though `string` is refused in every OTHER position. The emitter
// nulled the source's buffer and never recorded the move.
//
// It cost the consumer a real bug: a path string moved into one local and read two lines later through a
// `const ref` parameter wrote every frame of a video to `-00000`. A silent "" reads as "the flag was not
// passed", three files away from the move.
fn int32 main() {
    string a = "hello.ppm";
    string b = give a;
    isize n = a.length();   // ERROR: use of `a` after it was moved
    return cast<int32>(n) + cast<int32>(b.length());
}
